# Analytics data durability (CRITICAL)

Read before changing analytics, deploy, nginx, systemd, or storage. Full detail: `AGENTS.md` + `TODO.md`.

## This site’s store

- Live analytics = **PostgreSQL** volume `orthoandspinetools-main_postgres_data` (outside git / not under `dist/` or rsync `--delete`).
- Humans: `analytics_page_views` via JS beacon. Bots: `analytics_bot*` via nginx log tailer. Cursor: `analytics_bot_state.backfilled_at` gates one-shot backfill.
- Backups: `scripts/analytics-backup.sh` → `/mnt/HC_Volume_106016238/orthoandspinetools-backups/analytics/` (`analytics-latest.sql.gz`, ≥30d). Cron via `scripts/install-analytics-backup-cron.sh`.

## Before / after changes

- Before risky work: run backup; note dump size/mtime/sha256.
- After: `./scripts/analytics-durability-report.sh` and report viewsToday / views7d / bots.hits7d.

## Forbidden without explicit user approval

- Truncate/delete/replace analytics tables or dumps
- Clear `analytics_bot_state` / force full log re-backfill
- Move storage without copy + verify
- Store live analytics under deploy-cleaned paths
- `docker compose down -v`

## Semantics

- Do not invent historical human pageviews. UTC days. Do not “fix” accuracy by wiping. Scanners stay out of bot headlines.
